# Identify Repository Rule

Whenever a rule or action requires the agent to understand which repository it is operating in:
1. Run `git remote -v`.
2. Use the output to determine the repository name and remote URL.

## Example
If the output of `git remote -v` is:

```
origin  git@github.com:richardhannah/rfh_cursorrules.git
```

Then you know you are running in the `rfh_cursorrules` repository.


